Manual, end-to-end CLI reproduction of the defect this change fixes: a lock
holder that dies (kernel could recycle its pid to an unrelated process) is
correctly identified as dead and its lock is reclaimed - proven by directly
driving the shipped fm_lock_try_acquire / fm_lock_holder_is_current functions
against a real background holder process, not by reading source.

$ cd <worktree>
$ rm -rf /tmp/repro-home && mkdir -p /tmp/repro-home/state
$ LOCKDIR=/tmp/repro-home/state/.home-summary-refresh.lock
$ FM_ROOT_OVERRIDE="$PWD" FM_HOME=/tmp/repro-home bash -c '
    . "$1/bin/fm-wake-lib.sh"
    fm_lock_acquire_wait "$2"
    : > "$3"
    sleep 30
  ' _ "$PWD" "$LOCKDIR" /tmp/repro-marker &
HOLDER_PID=$!
# ... wait for /tmp/repro-marker to appear ...

$ ps -p "$HOLDER_PID" -o pid,ppid,command
  PID  PPID COMMAND
77554 77456 sleep 30

$ cat $LOCKDIR/pid
77554

$ cat $LOCKDIR/pid-identity
Tue Sep  1 23:53:30 2026     bash -c ...

# Confirms identity IS recorded at acquisition (point 1 of the intent).

$ kill -KILL 77554 ; wait 77554
$ kill -0 77554 2>/dev/null && echo alive || echo dead
dead

$ FM_ROOT_OVERRIDE="$PWD" FM_HOME=/tmp/repro-home FM_LOCK_STALE_AFTER=0 bash -c '
    . "$1/bin/fm-wake-lib.sh"
    if fm_lock_try_acquire "$2"; then rc=0; else rc=1; fi
    printf "rc=%s held=%s proof=%s recovered=%s\n" \
      "$rc" "${FM_LOCK_HELD_PID:-}" "${FM_LOCK_HOLDER_PROOF:-}" "${FM_LOCK_RECOVERED_PID:-}"
  ' _ "$PWD" "$LOCKDIR"
rc=0 held= proof=dead recovered=77554

# The dead holder's lock was correctly reclaimed (rc=0), with FM_LOCK_HOLDER_PROOF
# naming the evidence (dead) and FM_LOCK_RECOVERED_PID naming the abandoned pid,
# exactly matching the contract documented in fm_lock_holder_is_current.
